@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "SQL Basics Introduction";
}

<section>

    <!-- PAGE INTRODUCTION -->
    <div class="mb-5">

        <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            SQL Basics Introduction
        </h1>

        <p class="lead text-muted">
            SQL, which stands for Structured Query Language, is used
            to communicate with relational databases. SQL Server uses
            SQL commands to create, retrieve, modify and manage data
            stored in databases.
        </p>

    </div>


    <!-- WHAT IS SQL -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            What is SQL?
        </h2>

        <p>
            SQL is a standard language used to work with relational
            databases. It allows developers and database administrators
            to perform operations such as creating databases, creating
            tables, inserting records, retrieving data, updating records
            and deleting records.
        </p>

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Simple Definition
            </h5>

            <p class="mb-0">
                SQL is a language used to communicate with and manage
                data in a relational database.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- WHY SQL -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Why Do We Use SQL?
        </h2>

        <p>
            SQL provides commands that allow us to work with the data
            stored inside database tables.
        </p>

        <ul>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Create databases and tables
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Insert new records
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Retrieve data
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Update existing records
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Delete records
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Filter and sort data
            </li>

            <li>
                Manage database objects
            </li>

        </ul>

    </section>


    <!-- SQL AND SQL SERVER -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            SQL and SQL Server
        </h2>

        <p>
            SQL is the language used to communicate with a relational
            database. SQL Server is a relational database management
            system developed by Microsoft that understands and executes
            SQL statements.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL Server
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>
                                                        Application
                                                             ↓
                                                          SQL Query
                                                              ↓
                                                          SQL Server
                                                             ↓
                                                        Database Engine
                                                             ↓
                                                          Database
                                                             ↓
                                                           Result</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- FIRST SQL QUERY -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            First SQL Query
        </h2>

        <p>
            A simple SELECT statement can be used to retrieve data
            from a table.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>SELECT *
FROM Students;</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p class="mt-3">
            The above query retrieves all columns and all records from
            the Students table.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- SELECT EXAMPLE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Example
        </h2>

        <p>
            Suppose the Students table contains the following records:
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>StudentId</th>
                        <th>StudentName</th>
                        <th>Age</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>101</td>
                        <td>Rahul</td>
                        <td>22</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>102</td>
                        <td>Priya</td>
                        <td>21</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>103</td>
                        <td>Amit</td>
                        <td>23</td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

        <div class="code-block mt-4">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>SELECT StudentName, Age
FROM Students;</code></pre>

        </div>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4">
            Output
        </h5>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>StudentName</th>
                        <th>Age</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Rahul</td>
                        <td>22</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Priya</td>
                        <td>21</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Amit</td>
                        <td>23</td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- SQL STATEMENT STRUCTURE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Basic SQL Statement Structure
        </h2>

        <p>
            Most SQL statements follow a specific structure depending
            on the operation being performed.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>SELECT column_name
FROM table_name;</code></pre>

        </div>

        <div class="table-responsive mt-4">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>Keyword</th>
                        <th>Purpose</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>SELECT</strong></td>
                        <td>Specifies the columns to retrieve.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>FROM</strong></td>
                        <td>Specifies the table from which data is retrieved.</td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- BASIC SQL OPERATIONS -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Basic SQL Operations
        </h2>

        <p>
            SQL provides different commands for performing common
            database operations.
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>Operation</th>
                        <th>SQL Command</th>
                        <th>Purpose</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Create</td>
                        <td>CREATE</td>
                        <td>Create database objects.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Retrieve</td>
                        <td>SELECT</td>
                        <td>Retrieve data.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Insert</td>
                        <td>INSERT</td>
                        <td>Add new records.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Update</td>
                        <td>UPDATE</td>
                        <td>Modify existing records.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Delete</td>
                        <td>DELETE</td>
                        <td>Remove records.</td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- SQL QUERY FLOW -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            How a SQL Query Works
        </h2>

        <p>
            When a SQL query is executed, SQL Server processes the
            statement and returns the requested result.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL Server
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>User
  ↓
SQL Statement
  ↓
SQL Server
  ↓
Database Engine
  ↓
Table / Data
  ↓
Result</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- SQL EXAMPLE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Simple SQL Examples
        </h2>

        <div class="code-block mb-4">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>-- Retrieve data
SELECT * FROM Students;

-- Insert data
INSERT INTO Students
VALUES (104, 'Neha', 22);

-- Update data
UPDATE Students
SET Age = 23
WHERE StudentId = 104;

-- Delete data
DELETE FROM Students
WHERE StudentId = 104;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- IMPORTANT -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <div class="alert alert-warning border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Important
            </h5>

            <p class="mb-0">
                SQL statements should always be written carefully,
                especially UPDATE and DELETE statements. A missing
                WHERE condition can affect multiple records.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- SUMMARY -->
    <section class="mb-4">

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Summary
            </h2>

            <p class="mb-0">
                In this section, we learned what SQL is, why SQL is
                used, how SQL communicates with SQL Server, the basic
                structure of SQL statements and the common operations
                used to work with database data.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- PREVIOUS / NEXT -->

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center
                mt-5 pt-4 border-top">

